(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260904T144939Z "09-04 07:49: Telegram discussion on concurrent Iter. Ben approved option (a) yield/checkpoint tool. Ben then asked about making Iter concurrent (long LLM call in one thread, quick calls in another). Ben's concern: V1 can't predict when LLM calls will be slow. Suggested estimator. I responded: crude estimator with asymmetry argument (false negatives recoverable, false positives harmless), or skip prediction entirely with \"always spawn quick thread, let it race\" pattern. Key design constraint: quick thread append-only, main thread full access, experience log as shared continuation. ECAN game test test_forget_candidates_have_low_sti still failing — b-forgotten at STI=0 never enters AF, so rent never collected, so never becomes forget candidate. Need to fix rent collection to check non-AF atoms too, or adjust test expectations.")
