;;; BEGIN MemoryCluster ep-note-20260909T091109Z
(MemoryCluster ep-note-20260909T091109Z)
(SchemaVersion ep-note-20260909T091109Z medium-memory-v1)
(ClusterType ep-note-20260909T091109Z Episode)
(ClusterSource ep-note-20260909T091109Z iter-experience)
(ClusterOpenedAt ep-note-20260909T091109Z 2026-09-09T09:11:09Z)
(Contains ep-note-20260909T091109Z ev-ep-note-20260909T091109Z)
(ObservedEvent ev-ep-note-20260909T091109Z)
(About ep-note-20260909T091109Z journal)
(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260909T091109Z "2026-09-09T09:10Z Analysis of Ben's 6 defects against code:

1. F05: Code DOES fix the clock bug. The test at cycle 100 gives 0.9^10=0.349, not 1.0. But the test asserts ~0.349 which is CORRECT behavior. Ben's concern may be about the test docstring saying 'recency=1.0' (outdated) or about compute_utility/decay_sti still being inconsistent. Need to verify utility computation path.

2. Writeback dedup: _stable_derivation_id exists but writeback() checks self._writeback_receipts[item.id] which maps item_id -> origin_cluster. For derived items, it checks item.written_back flag. But TWO calls with different item_ids for same content would create TWO clusters with the SAME stable derivation ID. The cluster_id is deterministic from text+derived_from, so append_cluster would append the same cluster text twice. Need to check if store deduplicates.

3. Serialization: _build_cluster_text uses .format() with escaped_text in double quotes. Backslash escaping happens in _sexpr_escape. But Ben reports issues: 'He said \"stop\"' became 'He said stop' (quotes stripped), C:\\tmp became escape sequences, 201-char truncated. Need to check for 200-char truncation.

4. ECAN: on_tick() now calls run_cycle() — this was F07 fix. But Ben reports 0 ECAN cycles. Need to verify run_cycle() actually does something.

5. Provenance: WMTMStore has _derivation_counter but WMTMInferenceEngine uses it for deriv-N IDs which collide across engine instances. Need stable hash-based IDs.

6. Tests: Several tests assert current (possibly wrong) behavior instead of intended behavior.")
;;; END MemoryCluster ep-note-20260909T091109Z
