(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260909T091554Z "2026-09-09T09:15Z VERIFICATION RESULTS:

1. Cross-engine collision CONFIRMED: Engine2 deriving same text as Engine1 gets deriv-3 (not deriv-1), creating duplicate WMTM item. Store counter is shared but counter-based IDs are not content-deterministic.

2. Writeback dedup PARTIALLY WORKING: Store's _reject_duplicate_ids catches duplicate cluster IDs, but second item is NOT marked written_back (keeps retrying). Fix: check existing clusters before append.

3. Serialization: Escaping WORKS (quotes preserved in store). query_about('He') returns 0 because it does whole-value match not keyword search. Ben's issues may be from older commit d03e3a8 (wmtm-revision-plan branch, not our fix/wmtm-defects-v3).

4. ECAN cycle CONFIRMED WORKING: STI(belief) went from 0 to 73.99 after 2 ticks. run_cycle() is executing. But test_atoms_unchanged only checks count, not STI change.

5. F05 recency CORRECT: 0.9^10=0.349, not 1.0. Test docstring is misleading.

PLAN: Fix derivation IDs (hash-based), writeback idempotency (pre-check), reasoning event label, ECAN test, add proper regression tests.")
;;; END MemoryCluster ep-note-20260909T091554Z
