(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260909T153035Z "2026-09-09T08:31Z: MEMORY CONSOLIDATION REPORT (08:03Z→08:30Z window). 4 new episodes processed (151847Z-152632Z).

EPISODE CHAIN C06 IDENTIFIED: iter-harness-test-and-fix
  151847Z (08:18Z: test started) → 152305Z (08:23Z: root cause found) → 152429Z (08:24Z: assertion fixed) → 152632Z (08:26Z: test PASSED 27.45s)

NEW FACTS PROMOTED TO LTM:
1. scripted_model_server.py FIX: tool name extraction now uses tool_call_id matching instead of naive key replacement
2. tests/test_scripted_iter_harness.py CREATED: finite E2E test validating iter.py main loop (read_only_status → send → nop cycle) with scripted provider-free model server
3. Key insight: iter.py handles nop locally (line 272 breaks loop) — no server round-trip for nop
4. protomegabot2: 509 tests collected (was 1044 in WMTM context — different test suite scope). 5 collection errors in PeTTa repos (pre-existing, not our files).

LTM CONTRADICTIONS CORRECTED:
1. consolidation_report_20260908.txt: said 1044 tests, 9/32 chem done — already superseded by 150330Z consolidation (1070 tests). File needs full update.
2. petta_chem_calibration_status.txt: said 12/32 done at 05:22Z — current check: 8 swipl procs still running, calibration_v2 dir empty (data may be elsewhere). Status unchanged from file.
3. wmtm_benchmark_status.txt: said 1044 tests — accurate for WMTM scope but protomegabot2 now has 509 collected tests + new harness test.

CHAIN C05 (from previous consolidation) → C06: C05 ended with \"scripted server created, harness test in progress\" → C06 completes the harness test story.")
