(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260909T172205Z "10:21Z: WMTM repair work in progress. Read all 4 source files + tests. Key findings:

F05 clock bug: decay_sti() computes recency as 0.9^(age-last_used) but increments age AFTER computing recency. Test test_recency_cycle_100_bug asserts the CORRECT value (0.9^10) — but Ben says actual result is 1.0. Need to verify: the bug is that tick() calls decay_sti which sets last_used=age at admit time, so age-last_used=0 initially, but after 10 ticks without touch, age=10, last_used=0, giving 0.9^10=0.348. Test asserts 0.9^10 which IS correct. BUT Ben reports getting 1.0 — need to check if tick() calls touch() somewhere resetting last_used.

Writeback dedup: written_back flag exists on WMTMItem but need to verify writeback() checks it. _stable_derivation_id exists in wmtm_utility.

ECAN: coordinator on_tick() calls sync_from_store() but NOT run_cycle(). Test test_ecan_cycle_actually_runs checks STI change — but if ECAN doesn't run, STI won't change and test will FAIL. Need to add ecan.run_cycle() call in coordinator.

Next steps: 1) Fix F05 recency, 2) Fix writeback dedup+serialization, 3) Fix stable derivation IDs, 4) Fix ECAN lifecycle in coordinator, 5) Fix all tests asserting buggy behavior, 6) Run full suite, 7) Push to GitHub.")
;;; END MemoryCluster ep-note-20260909T172205Z
