(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260909T172602Z "10:25Z: Consolidation checkpoint. WMTM repair work status:

CODE READ COMPLETE - all 4 source files + tests examined.

Key findings from code review:
1. F05 clock: decay_sti() computes recency=0.9^(age-last_used) BEFORE incrementing age. Test test_recency_cycle_100_bug asserts 0.9^10 which seems correct. BUT Ben observed 1.0 — need to verify by running the actual code. May have been partially fixed since Ben's review commit d03e3a8.
2. Writeback dedup: written_back flag + _writeback_receipts dict exist. _stable_derivation_id() exists. BUT _build_cluster_text still creates reasoning events with EvidenceFor links (Ben's concern about fabricated evidence). Need to check if dedup actually works across engine instances.
3. ECAN: coordinator on_tick() already calls run_cycle() on line 90 — may have been added since Ben's review. Need to verify.
4. Serialization: _sexpr_escape exists but may still have issues with truncation, unmatched parens, etc.

NEXT: Run full test suite, identify failures, fix code + tests, push to GitHub.")
;;; END MemoryCluster ep-note-20260909T172602Z
