(About ep-note-20260911T050602Z journal)
(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260911T050602Z "05:06Z Sep 11 MEMORY CONSOLIDATION COMPLETE:

NEW LTM FILE: ltm_patterns_20260911.txt (17 patterns, up from 13)

NEW PATTERNS PROMOTED:
  P14: Progress rate much slower than estimated (supersedes P9)
  P15: Shell sleep does not work for long delays
  P16: Journal append is reliable communication fallback
  P17: Active shard attempt mapping (which attempts are running)

LTM PATTERN VERIFICATION RESULTS:
  P1 (swipl long queries): SUPPORTED + EXTENDED (28-37min observed)
  P2 (timeout): Still valid, no new evidence
  P3 (load mgmt): SUPPORTED (18+hr stable at load ~7)
  P4 (receipt count): SUPPORTED (+21 in 9.25hr despite 5 active)
  P5 (send() constraints): SUPPORTED (persistent failures 04:44-04:54Z)
  P6 (pathological queries): Still valid
  P7 (launcher reliability): SUPPORTED (PID 759790, 12hr uptime)
  P8 (memory accuracy): Still valid
  P9 (progress rate ETA): CONTRADICTED -> Superseded by P14
  P10-P13: All still valid

CONTRADICTION FOUND:
  C9: P9 ETA estimate (10-12h) was too optimistic. Actual rate: 3-4 receipts/shard/9.25hr. Root cause: L6 queries take 30-40min, not 17-25min. Resolution: P14.

NEW CAUSAL CHAINS:
  Chain4: 19:46Z (P9 ETA estimate) -> 05:01Z (contradiction: only 50% done) -> P14 (corrected rate) - self-correction chain
  Chain5: 04:44Z-05:01Z (send() failures) -> petta_append fallback -> P16 - resilience chain

STATUS FILES UPDATED: petta_chem_calibration_status.txt (05:01Z snapshot)")
;;; END MemoryCluster ep-note-20260911T050602Z
